I inverted the cached-type branch so the common uncached/profile-lookup path falls through instead of jumping, and combined the profile validity checks into one positive condition. This reduces taken branches on the hot decode path while preserving all invalid-input behaviour.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    if ( type == FIT_UINT8_INVALID )
    {
        if ( (profile != NULL) && (profileIndex < profile->numFields) )
            return profile->fields[profileIndex].type;

        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;
    }

    return type;
}
```